[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/llm_invoke.py:148-148 - The change always sends 'stream' field in the HTTP request body. Previously, when backend.stream was False, the field was omitted. Now it's explicitly set to false. This changes the HTTP request payload structure, which could break if the server expects the field to be absent when streaming is disabled, or if the server has a bug handling explicit false values. The OmniRoute server specifically is mentioned as picking SSE when the field is absent, so this change is designed to prevent that, but other servers might behave differently.
[RUNTIME] src/code_forge/llm_invoke.py:148-148 - The HTTP request is made via urllib.request.urlopen, which is a subprocess-level network call. If the server connection fails, times out, or returns an unexpected response format, the _parse_response_body function could fail to parse the response, leading to a non-JSON response error. The change ensures stream=false is always sent, but if the server still returns SSE format despite this, parsing will fail.
